21
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:33,290
I was made to hit in America

22
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:40,840
You're seriously thinking
about the revival of BECK,

23
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,670
so I wondered if I could help.

24
00:01:43,670 --> 00:01:45,840
And what did Chiba-kun say?

25
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:48,330
You will be dead!

26
00:01:50,010 --> 00:01:54,180
The conversation ended
in the worst way possible.

27
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:55,520
It's so like Chiba-kun.

28
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,520
-This is nothing to laugh at!
-Mmm.

29
00:01:58,520 --> 00:02:02,360
-Still...That ramen is bad!
-That ramen is bad!

30
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:07,720
"Condor Ramen"

31
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:09,390
Hello!

32
00:02:09,390 --> 00:02:11,720
-Hey...
-Chiba-kun, I...

33
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:12,750
Were you the one who sent Maho?

34
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,720
Were you the one who sent Maho?

35
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:16,120
Huh...Err, no...

36
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:19,420
Hah! Spouting her mouth off!

37
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:21,360
What did Maho say?

38
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,690
That there's no future
in bad-tasting ramen...

39
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:26,760
so I should join up
with BECK when they regroup.

40
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:29,930
That's all she kept saying.

41
00:02:29,930 --> 00:02:31,430
Chiba-kun!

42
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:32,400
Huh?

43
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:36,100
Let's revive BECK...one more time.

44
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:37,370
Huh?

45
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:41,880
Well...I'm the only one right now...

46
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:46,440
Sorry, but right now...
I can only think about ramen.

47
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:56,060
Hey, Koyuki!

48
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:59,890
Is my ramen...that bad?

49
00:02:59,890 --> 00:03:01,400
Yeah...

50
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:05,570
Are you serious about BECK?

51
00:03:05,570 --> 00:03:09,740
I have to be serious...
or there won't be another BECK!

52
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:11,670
I can come back?

53
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:15,740
I don't have to have a dream?

54
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:18,750
What're you saying, Chiba-kun?!

55
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:20,250
You're so late!

56
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:23,920
I've been regretting it since
the day after Grateful Sound...

57
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:26,750
Why'd that...

58
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:28,090
Chiba-kun!

59
00:03:28,090 --> 00:03:31,260
But I can't make it up with Ryusuke!

60
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:33,020
Chiba-kun...

61
00:04:18,410 --> 00:04:20,240
Taira-kun is awesome!

62
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:22,080
That band was something else!

63
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:24,850
Hurry it up before Taira leaves!

64
00:04:24,850 --> 00:04:27,580
Yeah...But if we're too hasty...

65
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:28,750
Taira-kun!

66
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,420
Hey, nice to see you.

67
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:33,090
Taira...Yoshiaki's calling for you.

68
00:04:33,090 --> 00:04:34,690
Be right there.

69
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:38,360
-Actually, I wanted to ask you
to return to BECK once...
-I got it.

70
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,090
-Huh?
-You're regrouping BECK?

71
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:41,100
Yes.

72
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:44,870
I was planning to agree only
if you came to see me.

73
00:04:44,870 --> 00:04:47,200
-Taira-kun...
-Hey, hey...

74
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:50,030
-Taira-kun!
-Idiot!

75
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:54,880
I'm a member of Heroes now,
so I can't commit immediately.

76
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:57,710
After the promotional tour,
I'll work it out with them.

77
00:04:57,710 --> 00:04:59,710
Taira-kun...

78
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:01,980
However...I'm agreeing to return...

79
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:05,720
...on the condition that all
five original members come back.

80
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,890
Huh?!

81
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:09,890
Otherwise, I want nothing
to do with this.

82
00:05:09,890 --> 00:05:11,390
Taira-kun...

83
00:05:11,390 --> 00:05:15,330
Sorry, but I'm busy. See ya.

84
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:19,600
Well then, the big problem
here is Ryusuke.

85
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,830
Yeah...

86
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:38,350
Maybe...he's no longer in Japan.

87
00:05:39,690 --> 00:05:43,350
Even if he's away,
I think our spirit is one.

88
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:52,530
"Saito Paper Company"

89
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:55,640
"Saito Paper Company"

90
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:55,640
Koyuki-kun, can you throw this out?

91
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,040
"Saito Paper Company"

92
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,040
Sure.

93
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:06,210
Koyuki-kun, can you go shopping?

94
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:08,550
I have a date with Momo-chan.

95
00:06:08,550 --> 00:06:09,980
All right.

96
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:16,650
"Chinese Restaurant Sing Lung"

97
00:06:34,070 --> 00:06:35,240
I'm back.

98
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,840
Oh, welcome home...

99
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,350
Was there a phone call for me?

100
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:40,510
No, there wasn't.

101
00:06:40,510 --> 00:06:41,670
I see.

102
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:45,010
Man, that was a fantastic
live performance!

103
00:07:45,010 --> 00:07:48,350
If you told me you were coming,
I'd have put you down as guests.

104
00:07:48,350 --> 00:07:52,520
Taira-san, will you
take a picture with me?

105
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:54,010
Sure.

106
00:07:55,690 --> 00:07:58,020
This is from Koyuki.

107
00:08:02,730 --> 00:08:04,370
Hey, Chiba!

108
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:08,370
Don't keep your fan waiting,
you sexy rocker!

109
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:09,630
Idiot!

110
00:08:11,710 --> 00:08:13,540
That Koyuki...

111
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:20,310
There's a strange rumor
spreading among the fans.

112
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:25,390
Yeah...Something about you
leaving Heroes after the tour.

113
00:08:25,390 --> 00:08:27,980
To rejoin BECK.

114
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,460
I mean, geez...

115
00:08:31,460 --> 00:08:35,990
Why would anyone quit Heroes,
which is gonna sell 200,000 CDs?

116
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:38,930
Hey, Taira!

117
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,670
Wanna listen?

118
00:08:40,670 --> 00:08:41,340
-Huh?
-Huh?

119
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:44,670
It's a rough cut.
But the genius shines through.

120
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:48,380
I'm amazed he wrote so many songs.

121
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:49,430
Huh?

122
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:53,010
For everything up to now,
thank you so much!

123
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:55,020
Think of me as a fool.

124
00:08:55,020 --> 00:08:57,150
But I'm going to return to BECK.

125
00:08:57,150 --> 00:08:58,850
-Are you kidding?!
-No shit?!

126
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,820
Hey, Ryusuke Minami!

127
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:31,890
Ho man, what a surprise!

128
00:09:31,890 --> 00:09:34,390
How long you been here
in New York?

129
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:35,980
Mr. Davis...

130
00:09:44,830 --> 00:09:46,830
Okay, Ryusuke Minami...

131
00:09:46,830 --> 00:09:50,170
If I can help, I'll give you a hand.

132
00:09:51,170 --> 00:09:53,670
I really appreciate it, Mr. Davis.

133
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:55,670
Doitashimashite. [You're welcome]

134
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:01,520
Yukio! Phone call!

135
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,850
Okay!

136
00:10:02,850 --> 00:10:04,180
Hello?

137
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:06,350
Huh?! Yeah.

138
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,710
Sorry to keep you waiting, Koyuki.

139
00:10:29,710 --> 00:10:32,550
-Saku!
-It took me a while
to save enough money.

140
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:34,550
You're late!

141
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,820
-Sorry.
-I was so worried!

142
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:38,820
Koyuki...

143
00:10:38,820 --> 00:10:41,660
You haven't been
in touch lately, either.

144
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:44,060
I wanted to come earlier...

145
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,330
Saku...

146
00:10:45,330 --> 00:10:46,660
Koyuki...

147
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:50,000
...just have to Stage Dive or Die

148
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Mind blower, a shower of sweat

149
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,500
Run towards a new world, my life

150
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:56,840
Those who seek it will be rewarded

151
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,070
Pass the hot shot

152
00:10:58,070 --> 00:11:00,270
Keep on coming, come on!

153
00:11:00,270 --> 00:11:02,680
Blow your mind

154
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,670
Squeeze your sweat yeah

155
00:11:06,410 --> 00:11:08,850
Your old man is stubborn.

156
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:14,020
I couldn't convince him,
had'ta run away.

157
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:15,020
Had'ta?

158
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:19,030
You can stay at my house for as long
as it takes to find an apartment.

159
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:20,530
I'm sa'happy.

160
00:11:20,530 --> 00:11:21,690
Sa'happy?

161
00:11:24,870 --> 00:11:29,200
Uh! Typhoon! Typhoon 24!

162
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,870
24-7! Non-stop...

163
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:33,710
Yukio, there's a phone call
from someone named Sato.

164
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:34,700
All right!

165
00:11:35,710 --> 00:11:37,040
Hello?

166
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:39,210
Congratulations on the revival of BECK!

167
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:40,810
O-Oh, thank you.

168
00:11:40,810 --> 00:11:43,350
I'll get right to the point.

169
00:11:43,350 --> 00:11:44,150
Yes?

170
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:48,060
There's an offer for BECK
for an American tour.

171
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:49,390
America?

172
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:02,240
Hello?

173
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,330
Hey, what's up?

174
00:12:04,570 --> 00:12:06,510
I heard about you from John.

175
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:07,740
I want to make a deal with you.

176
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:11,750
I have a most valuable tape here
which I got from Eddy Lee.

177
00:12:11,750 --> 00:12:12,680
I'll give you this,

178
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:16,750
instead I want you to leave
Mongolian Chop Squad alone forever.

179
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,920
Right. Some deal...

180
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:22,590
I'll bring the tape to
your hotel tonight anyway.

181
00:12:22,590 --> 00:12:25,020
You sure are a crazy dumb ass.

182
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:28,860
If you never change

183
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:33,360
I think there is no way my life fizzle out

184
00:12:36,270 --> 00:12:38,970
You open up the door with negative aura

185
00:12:38,970 --> 00:12:39,870
(I'm fed up fed up fed up)

186
00:12:39,870 --> 00:12:41,710
You say future is murky indeed...

187
00:12:41,710 --> 00:12:43,380
I'm sick of hearing gripe.

188
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:45,880
An American tour?!

189
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,210
That's unbelievable!

190
00:12:47,210 --> 00:12:48,880
Does that mean we
can throw television sets

191
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:50,880
out the window like
Lead Zeppelin and the Stones...

192
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:54,990
and fly around in groovy jets and stuff?

193
00:12:54,990 --> 00:13:00,550
Idiot! It's a hard tour...driving across
ten cities to perform in rock venues.

194
00:13:02,230 --> 00:13:05,070
-Ohh...
-Still, it's unbelievable.

195
00:13:05,070 --> 00:13:06,000
A band member of
a group called F.V.E.

196
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:10,240
Saw us at Grateful Sound
and made the offer.

197
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:13,070
-We've gotta do it!
-Think carefully!

198
00:13:13,070 --> 00:13:14,070
Huh?!

199
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:18,010
Without Ryusuke...it's too risky
for BECK to do an American tour.

200
00:13:18,010 --> 00:13:18,750
But...

201
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:21,980
It's not like us to turn down
a chance like this!

202
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:23,420
But it's dangerous.

203
00:13:23,420 --> 00:13:24,590
America, huh...

204
00:13:24,590 --> 00:13:28,180
-We'd better get passports.
-Does that cost money?

205
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:34,600
Summer vacation ended with BECK
rehearsals day in and day out.

206
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,930
Man, look how dark you got!

207
00:13:35,930 --> 00:13:37,360
And you're so white!

208
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:40,030
-Shaddup!
-Koyuki-kun, Saku-chan told me...

209
00:13:40,030 --> 00:13:42,370
But are you really
dropping out of school?

210
00:13:42,370 --> 00:13:43,200
Yeah.

211
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,040
Koyuki-kun...

212
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:47,710
I was hoping to
just fade out slowly...

213
00:13:47,710 --> 00:13:50,710
But with the American tour coming up,
I figured it's good timing.

214
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:52,880
Aww...It'll be lonely without you guys.

215
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,210
Sorry.

216
00:13:54,210 --> 00:13:55,720
America, huh?

217
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,710
It's too far, I can't go.

218
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,620
Farewell!

219
00:14:06,730 --> 00:14:09,900
This is an announcement
from the Student Council.

220
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:12,570
On the 26th from 3pm...

221
00:14:12,570 --> 00:14:13,570
...my sister.

222
00:14:13,570 --> 00:14:14,740
...my sister.

223
00:14:13,570 --> 00:14:14,740
We began exhausting live performances
to prepare for the American Tour.

224
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:17,340
In this world, which everyone is lonely.

225
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:17,340
We began exhausting live performances
to prepare for the American Tour.

226
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:19,410
In this world, which everyone is lonely.

227
00:14:19,410 --> 00:14:20,670
Yeah.

228
00:14:22,910 --> 00:14:24,910
If you are at a loss as to what to do.

229
00:14:24,910 --> 00:14:25,910
Raise you stiff middle finger.

230
00:14:25,910 --> 00:14:28,580
It will know which way the wind blows.

231
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:31,590
Our last performance was at the Marquee.

232
00:14:31,590 --> 00:14:34,250
Our next live performance in town...

233
00:14:34,250 --> 00:14:36,260
None!

234
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:43,030
Because BECK is starting a grueling 50-day,
46-city tour of the United States!

235
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:47,360
-BECK is the best!
-Chiba!

236
00:14:53,210 --> 00:14:57,710
Uh! Typhoon! Typhoon 24!

237
00:14:57,710 --> 00:14:58,210
24-7! Non-stop...

238
00:14:58,210 --> 00:15:02,550
24-7! Non-stop...

239
00:14:58,210 --> 00:15:02,550
For this last live performance,
Chiba dove into the audience for the close.

240
00:15:02,550 --> 00:15:04,640
Man, that was painful! Yes.

241
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:08,920
Huh? How was BECK?

242
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,660
Your guitar was great.

243
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,160
Really?

244
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,330
Yeah.

245
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:16,160
See ya.

246
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:18,500
Koyuki, wasn't that...

247
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,400
Hyodo. He was here as a guest.

248
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,840
Is he in a band?

249
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:26,740
They disbanded recently
and he's looking for new members.

250
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,580
Oh...

251
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:30,580
He said good luck
on our American Tour.

252
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:32,340
Oh yeah?

253
00:15:35,420 --> 00:15:36,580
Don't kid yourself!

254
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:38,190
I guess taking off for two months is...

255
00:15:38,190 --> 00:15:40,020
Damn right!

256
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:41,520
Then I'll have to quit.

257
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:44,690
It's easy to replace
someone like you!

258
00:15:44,690 --> 00:15:47,860
Thank you for everything.

259
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:49,690
America, huh?

260
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:54,840
Don't lose to the guys over there!

261
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:56,370
Yes!

262
00:15:56,370 --> 00:15:57,600
Slip out of...

263
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:59,770
Slip out ob.

264
00:15:59,770 --> 00:16:00,600
Out of!

265
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:02,040
Out ob.

266
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:04,040
You're hopeless!

267
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,880
You leave tomorrow!

268
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:08,320
If you can't pronounce
something like this,

269
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,220
you'd better not go to America!

270
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,390
Well Maho, you have
a hard time writing kanji.

271
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:15,890
We're not talking about me!

272
00:16:15,890 --> 00:16:19,760
Can't you be a little more gentle?

273
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:22,060
Well, excuse me
for not being gentle.

274
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:23,400
You're so petty!

275
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,990
You can drop dead
in America, Koyuki!

276
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:29,340
Stupid Maho!

277
00:16:31,070 --> 00:16:34,910
This is Tanaka...I had reservations
for 2 at 7 o'clock.

278
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:37,180
I'm sorry, but I have to cancel.

279
00:16:37,180 --> 00:16:38,350
Sorry.

280
00:16:38,350 --> 00:16:41,680
-Koyuki-kun, Maho forgot this.
-Huh?

281
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:43,210
This is...

282
00:16:44,220 --> 00:16:46,190
"Lesson Cassette: 'Slip Out', For Koyuki"

283
00:16:46,190 --> 00:16:47,810
"Lesson Cassette: 'Slip Out', For Koyuki"

284
00:16:46,190 --> 00:16:47,810
Maho...

285
00:16:48,190 --> 00:16:50,520
What a fool

286
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:54,190
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

287
00:16:54,190 --> 00:16:58,030
What it's like to be

288
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:04,040
Yukio, do you have your passport?

289
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:04,900
Yup.

290
00:17:05,870 --> 00:17:08,100
Then say goodbye to your father.

291
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,670
All right.

292
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,710
Did you call Grandma?

293
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:18,480
Yup.

294
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:27,060
No matter how many times
I look at it, it's a rough schedule.

295
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:29,400
Are we really gonna
make it in 50 days?

296
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,990
What will be will be!
That's all there is to know!

297
00:17:38,170 --> 00:17:40,540
Umm...Is this it?

298
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:43,870
Hey, it's so blurred!

299
00:17:44,850 --> 00:17:47,180
All right, there's the American continent!

300
00:17:47,180 --> 00:17:49,340
-Is that the wing of the jet?
-Uh-huh.

301
00:17:50,350 --> 00:17:55,020
David Eric of the popular
F.V.E. Band came to pick us up.

302
00:17:55,020 --> 00:17:56,510
He's out of focus.

303
00:17:57,520 --> 00:18:00,860
-This is an alien base.
-No, it's the L.A. Airport.

304
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:03,700
-Our hotel.
-Hey, pretty nice!

305
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:05,870
This was the only nice hotel.

306
00:18:05,870 --> 00:18:09,700
-Umm...Chiba-kun studying.
-Some study.

307
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:14,370
-We performed live here.
-It says Mongolian Chop Squad!

308
00:18:14,370 --> 00:18:16,210
But we just couldn't get it together.

309
00:18:16,210 --> 00:18:18,880
-The audience is looking down.
-Chiba is depressed.

310
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:20,400
Put it on spin!

311
00:18:21,380 --> 00:18:25,720
-These are members of other bands.
-Where are you, Koyuki?

312
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:30,060
-We traveled in this car.
-Saku's practically kissing the windshield!

313
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:33,230
-Hey, lots of people!
-We're not performing.

314
00:18:33,230 --> 00:18:35,900
-Look at the color of her hair!
-The Lizards. That's a guy.

315
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,460
Huh!?

316
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:40,030
We sold our CDs.
We sold quite a bit actually.

317
00:18:40,030 --> 00:18:41,500
Hmm...

318
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:45,010
-This is the car we traveled in.
-Looks so American.

319
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:47,500
-We're frogs.
-Silly!

320
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:51,010
-This is the car...
-I get it already!

321
00:18:51,010 --> 00:18:52,850
Hey, are they clowns?

322
00:18:52,850 --> 00:18:55,850
-This live was great.
-But I can't see you.

323
00:18:55,850 --> 00:18:59,350
It was great! Hurrah for Long Beach!

324
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:02,020
-We had a session together.
-What're you doing, Koyuki?

325
00:19:02,020 --> 00:19:04,020
-Oh, you had a flat tire.
-Yes.

326
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:05,620
That's Chiba-kun.

327
00:19:06,690 --> 00:19:09,860
-Look at the clouds!
-It's more awesome when
you actually see them.

328
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:11,200
Hmm...

329
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:15,040
-Oh, another session?
-Taira-kun was popular even in America.

330
00:19:15,040 --> 00:19:17,370
-And here's Chiba-kun.
-Koyuki, you look so cute.

331
00:19:17,370 --> 00:19:20,040
We were near total exhaustion.

332
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:23,040
-Looks like fun.
-A short moment of relaxation.

333
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:27,050
-Here we are in New York!
-This picture's so dark!

334
00:19:27,050 --> 00:19:29,480
-Taking a stroll in New York.
-Did you eat hot dogs?

335
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,720
Yup!

336
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:34,050
This is CBGB.
The audience is to the right.

337
00:19:34,050 --> 00:19:37,460
-And this is...
-That's the man...New York Punk.

338
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,760
Who is he?

339
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:43,830
He's Kevin Eric. The guitarist
and leader of F.V.E.

340
00:19:43,830 --> 00:19:46,330
-He's David's older brother.
-Hmm...

341
00:19:46,330 --> 00:19:50,170
-It's blurred again!
-Well, Kevin's a scary guy.

342
00:19:50,170 --> 00:19:52,510
-And this guy...
-Yup, that's...

343
00:19:52,510 --> 00:19:54,010
Umm...Texas, I think.

344
00:19:54,010 --> 00:19:56,340
-We even traveled
through a place like this.
-Hmm...

345
00:19:56,340 --> 00:20:00,180
-Golden Gate Bridge.
-That's San Francisco!

346
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:02,340
-And this is...
-Seattle.

347
00:20:03,350 --> 00:20:05,050
And that's Pike Place Market.

348
00:20:05,050 --> 00:20:06,680
-A supermarket?
-You can see fish jumping.

349
00:20:07,690 --> 00:20:08,850
And the Space Needle.

350
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:11,360
And Jimi Hendrix.

351
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:13,190
Chiba-kun had a dream.

352
00:20:13,190 --> 00:20:15,030
And he heard Jimi say,
"Let's meet at my grave."

353
00:20:15,030 --> 00:20:18,700
-Grave?
-And the day was September 18.

354
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:24,040
-The day mentioned in Ryusuke's message.
-And also, the day Jimi Hendrix died.

355
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:26,030
Koyuki, you're cut off.

356
00:20:27,040 --> 00:20:30,040
-This is Jimi Hendrix's grave.
-Hmm...

357
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:33,050
And...we found Ryusuke.

358
00:20:33,050 --> 00:20:35,050
Beck and Keith, too?

359
00:20:35,050 --> 00:20:36,380
Yep.

360
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:39,320
It's blurred again.

361
00:20:40,750 --> 00:20:42,960
Oh, this is the newspaper article.

362
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:47,160
-So Leon was arrested.
-And Ryusuke was right there.

363
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:50,000
I'm so glad he's alive!

364
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,330
-Oh, you saw this already.
-Yeah.

365
00:20:54,070 --> 00:20:58,170
And...we met up with Ryusuke,
who had Lucille,

366
00:20:58,170 --> 00:21:01,340
at the Crocodile Cafe in Seattle.

367
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:05,010
It was the first time all five members
were together since coming to America.

368
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:06,340
Now this is BECK!

369
00:21:07,350 --> 00:21:10,340
-Koyuki, let's do "Slip Out."
-Right.

370
00:21:44,050 --> 00:21:50,560
I don't know since when I changed
to such a cold-hearted guy.

371
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:56,730
I have to warm this frozen icy
lonely heart to thaw.

372
00:21:56,730 --> 00:22:02,740
I like being wrapped with warmness
more than anything else for sure.

373
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:11,410
I'm gonna make my coming days
to be filled with laughter and joy

374
00:22:12,750 --> 00:22:15,080
Hey, what're you doing?!

375
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:16,750
I let myself down that I'm more cruel
then I thought I would be.

376
00:22:15,080 --> 00:22:16,750
Stop teasing him!

377
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:19,740
I let myself down that I'm more cruel
then I thought I would be.

378
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:19,740
Shut up! Let's go, everyone!

379
00:22:23,260 --> 00:22:25,430
Beck! Come here!

380
00:22:25,430 --> 00:22:28,090
I told you,
you shouldn't go out alone.

381
00:22:28,090 --> 00:22:29,100
You...

382
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:31,030
You made me worry.

383
00:22:31,030 --> 00:22:33,760
A foreigner?

384
00:22:35,940 --> 00:22:38,200
Isn't this dog ugly?

385
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:42,230
Thank you for saving Beck.

386
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:45,000
Sorrow isn't what I am,
but its growing my sensation

387
00:22:46,070 --> 00:22:52,240
Regrets taught me how
to make any hard decisions.

388
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:58,580
Peace is always by my side
but I've never felt it once.

389
00:22:58,580 --> 00:23:05,590
Love is not the word only
for the sweet romance. Yeah.

390
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:11,760
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

391
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:18,100
And I'm scared to keep on
going on my way. Yeah.

392
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:24,280
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

393
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:29,870
And I tell myself
I'm special till the end.

394
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:52,900
I don't give my heart to no one
cause I don't wanna waste my time.

395
00:23:52,900 --> 00:24:01,000
I tried to love this loneliness
to slip out of lonesome hole.
